CORE
main.py
--unwind 6
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
PLR 5.3: importing a user module executes its body. The imported module's
non-literal globals (a comprehension, an arithmetic constant, a list built
by append) were never initialised, and its function bodies could not resolve
them. Its top level now runs before the importer's body, with __name__ bound
to the module name (so its __main__ guard does not fire).
